[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="DialogueResource" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://core/story/dialogue_resource.gd" id="1_d"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_d")
text = "Narration|gate||Then came a sage to the palace gate, and with him the first step of a long road.
Dasharatha|||Vishvamitra! Rain has come to a dry field. Ask, great one. Whatever you ask is already given.|joy
Vishvamitra|||You have said it, King, and a king's word is a vow. Hear what I ask before you say it again.|calm
Vishvamitra|||Two rakshasas, Maricha and Subahu, rain blood upon my sacrifice. My vow forbids me to curse them.|resolve
Vishvamitra|||Give me Rama, your eldest, for ten nights. He alone can end this.|resolve
Dasharatha|||Rama?|concern
Dasharatha|||He is not yet sixteen. He has never seen a battle. Take my army. Take me. Not my son.|grief
Dasharatha|||I waited half my life for him. Do not ask me to give him to the night.|grief
Vishvamitra|||A king who promises and then bargains has forgotten whose son he is.|anger
Vishvamitra|||So be it. I will go as I came. Live happily among your kinsmen, King of the Raghus.|anger
Narration|gate||The earth trembled at the sage's anger, and even the gods grew still.
Vasishtha|||My king. You were born in the line of Ikshvaku. Truth is your inheritance. Do not cast it away.|concern
Vasishtha|||This sage is master of every astra known to gods or men. Rama is safer at his side than behind any wall of ours.|calm
Vasishtha|||He does not ask for Rama because he needs a guard. He asks because he means to give him something.|calm
Dasharatha|||Rama. Lakshmana. Come to me.|grief
Rama|||Father, I will return. Bless the bow, not only the boy.|resolve
Lakshmana|||Where my brother walks, I walk.|resolve
Dasharatha|||Go then, both of you. And come back to me.|grief
Vishvamitra|||Come, princes. The Sarayu is waiting, and so is what I have to teach you.|calm
Narration|gate||So the two princes walked out of Ayodhya behind the sage, bows on their shoulders, toward a forest no one entered."
